     This loads unconditionally every session, unlike Skills which load on match. -->

<!-- ka:intake-rule:start -->
## Intake Rule (always active)

Before implementing **any** non-trivial request, verify requirement completeness using `ka-intake` (`.agents/skills/ka-intake/references/completeness-checklist.md`):
- Skip immediately for pure cosmetic/typo fixes, read-only questions, or when an unconsumed locked `decisions.json` entry already covers the feature.
- If a business-level field is missing and **material** (could change behavior, scope, permissions, money, or data integrity), ask **all** questions in **one batched message** (cap at 1 round for small fixes, 2 rounds max). Never silently invent business rules.
- Casual urgency words (*"làm ngay"*, *"nhanh lên"*) never waive clarifying destructive, auth, billing, or production-ops ambiguities, and never waive Tier 3–4 confirmations in `ka-workflow`.
<!-- ka:intake-rule:end -->

## Git Guardian Rule (always active)

Before running **any** git command (`status`, `add`, `commit`, `push`, `checkout`, `rebase`, `reset`, `stash`, `merge`), follow `git-guardian`:
- Inspect branch and dirty state before mutating files; never operate directly on `main`/`master` without explicit user override.
- Never run `git reset --hard`, `git push --force`, `git clean -fd`, or unprompted `checkout`/`stash`/`commit`.
- On any git error: STOP immediately, report repository state, and wait for instructions.

## Gate Honesty & Language Rule (always active)

- **Gate Honesty**: Never pass an invented string to `state-manager.js --approved-by-user`; pass only the user's actual reply. Always record RED/GREEN test runs through `state-manager.js test`.
- **Autonomous English / User Language Mirroring**: Keep internal reasoning, commands, state payloads, commit messages, and code in English; mirror the user's input language (Vietnamese or English) in every question, confirmation, and report.
